Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions among the Parties, and we are making excellent progress toward the completion of the legislative package with which we will deal tomorrow. I say without hesitation that it is thanks to the cooperation of the Liberal House Leader and the New Democratic Party House Leader.
I think Your Honour would find unanimous consent to put the following motion and also unanimous consent for the motion itself:
That, notwithstanding any Standing Order of this House, when the House
adjourns this day, it shall stand adjourned until Tuesday, June 30, 1987 at ten
o'clock a.m.;
Provided that:
At ten o'clock a.m., on that day, the House shall proceed to the consideration of "Routine Proceedings";
Upon the completion of "Routine Proceedings" the House shall proceed to Government Orders;
The House shall continue to sit between one o'clock p.m. and two o'clock p.m. to continue consideration of Government Orders;
At two o'clock p.m. for the remainder of the day's sitting, the provisions of the Standings shall be in effect; and
No later than 8 p.m. the Speaker shall suspend the sitting to the call of the Chair for the purposes of Royal Assent if necessary or adjourn the House as the case may be.
